sequenceDiagram
    participant W as Waiter<br/>(POS UI)
    participant C as Order<br/>Controller
    participant OS as Order<br/>Service
    participant RD as RecipeDeduction<br/>Service
    participant IR as Ingredient<br/>Repository
    participant IL as InventoryLedger<br/>Service
    participant EP as OrderEvent<br/>Publisher
    participant AL as InventoryAlert<br/>Service

    W->>C: 1. POST /api/orders<br/>(tableId, items[], customerPhone)
    C->>OS: 2. submitOrder(request,<br/>waiterPrincipal)

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
    Note over OS,IL: Single @Transactional boundary — steps 3 to 19
    OS->>OS: 3. tableService.openTableForOrder(tableId)
    Note over OS,RD: SELECT … FOR UPDATE on the table row —<br/>status becomes OCCUPIED
    OS->>OS: 4. customerRepository.findByPhoneNumber<br/>— creates a Walk-in customer if unknown
    OS->>OS: 5. menuItemRepository.findById per line<br/>— rejects an unavailable item
    OS->>RD: 6. deductForOrder(List&#60;DeductionLine&#62;)
    Note over OS,RD: @Transactional(REQUIRED) — joins the same<br/>transaction as OrderService, no new tx
    RD->>RD: 7. recipeRepository.findByMenuItemId(id) per line<br/>— List of Recipe with quantityRequired,<br/>summed per ingredient
    RD->>IR: 8. findAllByIdForUpdate(sorted ids)
    Note over RD,IL: SELECT … FOR UPDATE in ascending id order —<br/>blocks concurrent transactions, avoids deadlock
    IR-->>RD: 9. locked Ingredient rows
    RD->>RD: 10. validate stock ≥ required, every ingredient
    Note over RD,IL: Any shortfall raises InsufficientStockException →<br/>HTTP 409 and the whole transaction rolls back
    RD->>RD: 11a. newStock = current − (qty × recipeQty)
    RD->>IR: 11b. ingredientRepository.save(ingredient)
    RD->>IL: 12. recordRecipeDeduction<br/>(ingredient, −qty, newStock)
    IL-->>RD: 13. append-only ledger row
    RD->>EP: 14. publishMenuItemAvailabilityChanged<br/>— only if stock reached zero
    RD->>RD: 15. check stock vs reorder_level / zero, then<br/>publishEvent(ReorderThresholdBreachedEvent)
    RD-->>OS: 16. deduction complete
    OS->>OS: 17. orderRepository.save(order) — status PENDING
    OS->>EP: 18. publishNewTicket(order, tableNumber)
    OS->>EP: 19. publishTableStatusChanged(table)
    end

    Note over OS,EP: Transaction commits on return — order, stock and ledger durable.<br/>Steps 18 and 19 are dispatched inside the transaction —<br/>the stock<br/>alert below is the one deferred to AFTER_COMMIT.
    EP-->>W: 20. STOMP /topic/kitchen and /topic/tables
    OS-->>C: 21. OrderResponse (id, status, items)
    C-->>W: 22. 201 Created — order confirmed
    Note over W,EP: Kitchen Display receives the KitchenTicketMessage over the WebSocket — the ticket appears in the "New" lane

    AL->>AL: 23. onReorderThresholdBreached(event)
    Note over AL: @Async @TransactionalEventListener<br/>(AFTER_COMMIT) — own thread, after commit
    AL->>AL: 24. handleReorderBreach(id, severity)<br/>— drafts a Purchase Order if none is in flight
    AL->>EP: 25. publishStockAlert(ingredient, severity, draftPoId)
